[[2047,127,33554432,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The control unit for the Air Bag system \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\ncontrolled by the ignition (INT) at pin 5 from a line protected\nby shunt fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B32</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of supplementary\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99.</p><p>Pin 40 is connected to a specific earth \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>When frontal impact of a certain severity (depending on the software setting) is detected, the control unit sends control signals to set off the modules:</p><ul><li>to driver&#x27;s airbag <strong>Q9</strong> , through a clockspring on\nthe steering wheel <strong>Q10</strong> (from pins 11 and 10):</li><li>to passenger side air bag <strong>Q11</strong> (from pins 13 and\n14);</li><li>to the pretensioners on the driver&#x27;s side <strong>Q20</strong> (from\npins 1 and 2) and the passenger side <strong>Q21</strong> (from pins 3 and\n4).</li></ul>"],[2047,7,33554432,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>Pins 15 and 37 are connected to the sensor\nin the seat for disabling the passenger Air Bag \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K65</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"],[2047,127,33554432,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>Pins 6 and 12 are connected to the passenger\nAir Bag disabling switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H75</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Side impact detection sensors \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K66</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (driver&#x27;s\nside) and \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K67</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               (passenger side) send signals to pins 22, 24\nand 23, 25 respectively of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>When side impact of a certain severity (dependent on the software setting) is detected, the control unit sends control signals to set off the modules:</p><ul><li>to the driver&#x27;s side Air Bag <strong>Q30</strong> (from pins 16\nand 17);</li><li>to the passenger side Air Bag <strong>Q31</strong> (from pins 18\nand 19);</li></ul><p>The two side Air Bags are connected to earth \n\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>When the system autodiagnostic function\ndetects a failure or an impact is detected, the control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends\na signal from pin 7 for the &quot;Air Bag failure&quot; warning\nlight, located in check instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . This signal turns\non the warning light because instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied via\nthe ignition (INT) by a line protected by control lighting fuse\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              up\nto 2/99 or from fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of supplementary fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99.</p><p>Self-diagnostic data may be read by connecting\nthe unit to connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : this receives signals from pin\n9 of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               through the appropriate tester line.</p><p>Pin 33 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends the signal for\nthe &quot;passenger Air Bag disabled&quot; warning light, located\nin the speedometer \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . This signal causes the warning light\nto come on because instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied via the ignition\n(INT) from a  line protected by the control light fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up\nto 2/99 or by fuse\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              of supplementary fuse box\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              from\n2/99.</p>"]]